---
import '../styles/about.css';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="A little about me — the person behind the blog.">
  <div class="content-wrapper">
    <div class="page-header">
      <h1>About Me</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="about-content">
      <p>
        Hi! I'm Akshat Ayush. I'm a curious person who thinks too much, drinks too much coffee,
        and has opinions about things that probably don't matter but feel very important at 2am.
      </p>

      <p>
        I studied Computer Science with a specialization in Artificial Intelligence at the University
        of Toronto. Originally from Patna, now based in Toronto — a city that's good for long walks,
        good food, and the kind of cold that makes you productive indoors.
      </p>

      <p>
        This site is my little corner of the internet — a place to write about whatever I'm
        currently obsessed with, share things I've built, and leave a trail of the thoughts
        that pass through my head.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm into</h2>
      <p>
        My interests orbit a few recurring themes: ML and AI (both the technical craft and the
        larger questions about where it's all heading), economics and systems thinking (why things
        work the way they do, and why they often don't), cooking (the closest thing to debugging
        you can eat), and music (which I consume in unreasonable quantities). I like things that
        reward patience — ideas that get more interesting the longer you sit with them.
      </p>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>
        I build things with code, mostly at the intersection of machine learning and software
        engineering. I'm drawn to problems where the interesting part isn't just getting something
        to work, but understanding <em>why</em> it works — and what happens at the edges where
        it doesn't.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        You can find me on <a href="https://github.com/akshatayush" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
        I like interesting conversations — about ideas, projects, or whatever rabbit hole you're
        currently in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
